STATIC (tip source; B did not edit)
---

File: `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo`

| Site | Fact |
|------|------|
| L6–7 | comment: line-start `// SECRET: <ident>` → `__sec__name=1` |
| L8 | needle is `"// " + "SECRET:"` (exact; not mid-token) |
| L14–21 | `at_line` iff `i==0` **or** previous char is `"\n"` |
| L22–32 | match needle only when `at_line` |
| L35–42 | skip `" "` / `"\t"` after colon |
| L43–65 | ident class `_A-Za-z0-9` (start+cont same set) |
| L65 | `let name = str_slice(src, start, k)` — A's OWN; not re-proved |
| L66–69 | `name == ""` → `ERR\tsecret\tinvalid name …` + `process_exit(1)` |
| L70–72 | `c_env_put(env, "__sec__"+name, "1")` then `__secref__` |
| L73 | `i = k` then loop — **next** line-start `// SECRET:` still scanned |

So:

1. **Multi-name:** each successful line-start match `c_env_put`s both
   `__sec__` and `__secref__`. The walker continues at `k` (after the
   ident), so a later line-start needle is still found. Two tags ⇒ two
   env roots.
2. **Empty fail-closed:** after skip-ws, if `start==k` then `name==""`
   and the function **exits 1** before any further emit. Punct (`!`)
   is not `is_al` → same empty path.
3. **Midline ignore:** if previous char is not `\n` (and `i≠0`), the
   needle is never compared. `// Mention // SECRET: x` and
   `let x = "ok"; // SECRET: x` do not tag.

