---
RESIDUAL (honest; do not close)
---

1. **Column-0 line-start only.** `at_line` requires `i==0` or prev
   `"\n"`, then the **next** chars must be `// SECRET:`. Indented
   `    // SECRET: x` is **not** a tag (isolated `indented.oo` emit
   rc=0). Path A = column-0 after newline, not “first non-ws on line”.
   Midline OWN is still met. Did not patch.

2. **Ident class includes digits at start** (`is_al` is one set).
   `// SECRET: 1x` would tag `1x`. Not this OWN (empty-name is
   fail-closed; start-digit is a later hygiene).

3. **Empty exits the whole compile.** A later valid `// SECRET: ok`
   after an empty directive is never reached. Fail-closed as specified.

4. **7.10 slice hygiene is A's OWN.** Tip source L65 is `str_slice`.
   Live host binary may still be pre-slice. B proved **behavior**, not
   allocator math. Smoke script residual comment still mentions concat.

5. **Full IFC / `${}` interp / `#[Secret]` / macro-body SECRET** —
   `SECRET_TAINT.oot`. Not this parse-env contract.

6. **Leading BOM / CR-only line breaks.** `at_line` keys on `"\n"`
   only. `\r` alone would not start a line. Adjacent (8.6 strip_cr),
   not 7.10 B.

